  'ex.r.stand': 'R code (stand model) redoes the training and the plot-level cross-validation in R: the same units and targets, NLS (nls), SUR, log-OLS or CDFR (Levenberg–Marquardt written out in the script); if you made a prediction on the prediction tab, the responses and recovered parameters for that stand. The site\'s tests check in R at every release that this code gives the tool\'s numbers.',
  'ex.r.boot': 'The R code redoes the bootstrap runs you did for this fit (p-values, intervals) in R: the generator is the tool\'s, so the same seed gives the same replicates; refits with fitdistrplus. Run the bootstrap first. The site\'s tests check in R at every release that this code gives the tool\'s numbers.',
  'ex.r.rec': 'The R code redoes this card\'s recovery in R with the same summaries (written into the script, no data file needed; the Johnson SB cards use the nleqslv package). The site\'s tests check in R at every release that this code gives the tool\'s numbers.',
  'ex.r': 'R code (.R)', 'ex.r.note': 'The R code redoes the fitting run with the fitdistrplus package and the same settings: the same units, diameters or classes, distributions (with the tool\'s parameters), methods, fixed parameters and thresholds; KS, A², W², AIC/BIC. The recovery cards, the bootstrap tab and the stand models have their own R code. The data are not embedded; change the file name at the top of the script to the path of your file (an approved package or pasted table comes along as a CSV file). The site\'s tests check in R at every release that this code gives the tool\'s numbers.',
